# Independent review record

Reviewer: fresh ec_revisor context, separate from implementation. This record is
materialized by the coordinator from the reviewer's messages; it does not imply
that the coordinator performed the independent review. No reviewer code edits.

Scope of first pass: governance envelopes/traceability, documentation and export
links,17-skill proposal/applied bytes, bounded Rust/UI changes. The new audit
succession gate was still being implemented and is explicitly excluded from this
first-pass approval.

The reviewer independently compared 28 envelopes and 40 moved observation objects,
confirming exact JSON preservation, only 3 APPROVED→UNVERIFIED changes and no
promotion/historical rehash. It checked 17 proposal preimages/postimages and their
applied bytes. Validator freshness/convergence passed; design generation passed;
114/114 contrast pairs passed; 43 actual feature directories were indexed. Cached
dependency-font TTF/source hashes matched. These observations are inspection and
focused execution, not native or product-wide acceptance.

Four substantive findings were returned and corrected:

1. Focus style erased selected Navigation(true) background. The final style
   preserves surface_selected and the new regression checks selected versus
   unselected under all enabled focus states/themes.
2. Input style erased Disabled appearance. The final shared input_style keeps
   recessed/muted disabled state without adding callbacks or re-enabling editing.
3. PE-03 still required stacking below 900 while source used fixed 210/280 sidebar.
   The current spec explicitly names the successor; native acceptance is not renewed.
4. New structure/feature-index links targeted product paths excluded from a
   governance copy. They now use textual full-checkout references, with no broader
   allowlist or link exemption.

Low-priority wording fixes also applied: old Windows chrome number, mixed-language
local-task sentence, active limitation describing vanished current bindings,
PostgreSQL capability pointer, and focused-base prose now preserving selected
surface. Their final source identities are in final-ui-inputs.json or the bounded
succession inventory. Earlier visual-report hashes/results remain historical.

Final first-pass verdict: no remaining substantive defect identified in the
corrected source/documentation/skill lot, within its stated scope. Native layout,
AT, SVG fit and the new succession gate remain outside this verdict until the
corresponding observations exist. New gate review will be appended separately.

## Final independent gate review

The same independent reviewer returned a favorable final verdict, with no remaining
finding in the examined bounded gate. It inspected audit_revision.py, Windows/OSV/log
hooks, link helper, registries, 47 preimages and tests. It confirmed 46 successors and
20 mandatory origins with fixed inventories/hashes; unknown buffers do not normalize;
current drift, missing files, downgrade and symlinks are rejected. The intermediate
project bridge requires the authenticated current terminal and preserves historical
hashes. The copy helper retains exactly two preexisting DESIGN destinations and
requires an explicit receipt and authenticated content. The historical test keeps
the original 21 records and 12 excluded-target assertions.

Executed independently, with PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1, all exit 0:

- `python3 -m unittest discover -s tools/governance/tests -p test_audit_revision.py -v`: 7 PASS.
- Same discovery command with `test_windows_design_revision.py`: 5 PASS.
- `PYTHONPATH=tools/governance/tests python3 -m unittest test_historical_link_resolution.HistoricalLinkTests.test_all_five_reviewed_locations_and_unlisted_identity -v`: 1 PASS.
- `python3 tools/governance/scripts/check-ox.py`: PASS.

Final hashes match succession.md, including audit code 330c9f17…, helper 257888da…,
test 91990d3a… and registry fc5127b5…. The reviewer inspected the isolated PASS log,
receipt, absent application/ and byte equality of the five modules/registry between
copy and source; it did not rerun that copy. The Python audit hook covers observed
Python accesses and is not an OS sandbox. This gate verdict does not approve native
behavior, public distribution or all semantics of the 46 documents. No reviewer file
edits occurred. AC-04 was returned to the independent validator for its decision.
